God’s anger lasts only a moment, but I enjoy His favour all
my lifetime. Weeping may remain for a night, but rejoicing
comes in the morning. (Ps. 30:5 NIV).

The Lord favours me, and makes my mountain stand firm.
He does not hide his face from me so I am never dismayed.
(Ps. 30:7 NIV).

I get lands, possessions and accomplishments, not by my
sword, sweat or strength or arm but God’s Right Hand, His
arm, and the light of His countenance because He always
favours me. (Ps. 44:2-3 NKJV).

So shall the King greatly desire my beauty. He is my Lord, I
worship Him. People shall bring gifts to me; even the rich
and great people will bring gifts to intreat my favour. (Ps.
45:11-12 KJV paraphrased).

In God’s name I shall rejoice all day: and in His
righteousness I shall be exalted. For He is the glory of my
